  "Question": "If \\(991 + 993 + 995\\) \\(+ 997 + 999\\) \\(= 5000 - N,\\) then \\(N = \\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(15\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Five copies of \\(1000\\) would total \\(5000\\). The given addends are smaller than \\(1000\\) by \\(9,7,5,3,1\\), respectively, so their total falls short of \\(5000\\) by the sum of these differences:\n\\[\n991+993+995+997+999\n=5000-(9+7+5+3+1)\n=5000-25.\n\\]\nThe question calls this shortfall \\(N\\), so \\(\\boxed{N=25}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
